Lorebook parity with SillyTavern, meaning search limits, blue entries never cut

Exam on the owner's settings (same chat and message in ST and here, Gemini 3.5 flash lite,
Cohere vectors): 301 lore entries match by keywords, same order and size.

- retrieval: equal-Order entries from ST files go in reverse activation order, chain text is the
  whole buffer, Latin keys by ending only (s/es/ed/ing), ST "match whole words" for Latin
  one-word keys (setting whole_words, with_latin_whole), blue entries are never cut by the budget
- meaning search: at most meaning_max (7) per reply above the threshold; Cohere threshold 0.40
- card book entries keep ST's own sticky (0 when absent), ST chat reasoning goes back as <think>
- assembly: \r removed, lore of the author's note goes without note text
- tokens: Latin 7 letters per token, Cyrillic 3.5, punctuation 0.75 (python and js)
- devtools: affected.py finds the tests a change can break (fast tier + affected files)
- docs: ST_PARITY, HOW_IT_WORKS, AGENTS (run affected while working, full suite once at the end)
